@video{constructivemindest2019,
  entrysubtype = {video},
  title = {How to {{Understand}} and Remember Everything You Read and {{Learn}}},
  editor = {{Constructive Mindest}},
  editortype = {director},
  date = {2019},
  url = {https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m73x_6yqNWk},
  urldate = {2023-02-27},
  abstract = {Here are tips on how to understand and remember everything you read and learn. These reading strategies can help you absorb information like never before. Master these steps and you won't forget the important information that you had read. This video contains simple tricks to read smarter that can help anybody to learn effectively and easily, study effectively, memorize, remember lectures, train brain to absorb information and remember everything you read. Transcript: Did you know that it takes approximately 10000 hours to become an expert at something? Which means it takes about 3 years to master something if you do it for 10 hours every single day. That's quite a long time isn't it? But it is possible to become a genius at whatever you do, by spending much lesser than 10000 hours. How? By increasing your brain's capacity to absorb more information, that's what this video is majorly based on. Taking in information and being able to access it from your brain at all times, is the beginning of mastery. There's no end to learning, and if used properly, these methods can help you increase your brain's capacity of absorbing information by a massive amount and train you to become an expert learner. Let's get started. Method 1. Put your imagination into action. Why do we forget a great amount of what we've read but remember almost everything from a movie? Of course it is because the movie has a visual representation, but there is something more important than that. We remember most of the movie because we enjoy it. This technique can also be applied to remember something you reed or learn. Enjoying the reading process is the key to make your learning more effective. This is very important, we learn the most when we are enjoying the process. And it depends on how you use your imagination to make it more enjoyable. For example, if you are reading a story with two main characters, imagine them as two of your friends in real life, or one being you, and the other being your friend. Create a high detailed movie in your mind. This makes it funny, interesting and more enjoyable. Do not be discouraged if you don't have a great vivid imagination. It grows the more you use it. There's no limit to it. This is one of the reasons why reading is better than watching. Method 2. Pretend you're there. Dive into the subject by pretending you are there. This is possible by using the five senses of seeing, hearing, feeling, smelling, and tasting.  Suppose you are reading about a person driving a car, see the road, hear the traffic, feel the steering wheel, smell the car. This is basically taking your imagination to the next level and making it even more powerful. Doing this can be extremely helpful to keep yourself from all the distractions and concentrate on what you are reading at the moment.  Method 3. Teach what you have learned.  Teaching is learning for the second time and its the best way to learn. This is one such technique that can blend the information into your mind. Since the maximum amount of people go to the internet when they need to learn something, You can't always find someone to teach. So what can you do? You too, go to the internet. Find out websites like Yahoo answers, Fluther or Quora and find out topics you have learned about, answer the questions related to what you have learned or read about. Imagining to teach yourself by simplifying what you are learning, can also be helpful. Just talk to yourself like you are explaining it to your friend. Method 4. Make use of the times when you're on auto pilot. We spend most hours of the day on auto pilot mode. Meaning we are not completely conscious while doing daily tasks such as gardening, bathing, cooking or taking a walk. Most parts of our brain don't need to be active while doing such simple things. The fourth trick is to make use of times like these, by giving your brain some work, by remembering what you had learned. Using this method whenever your mind is free, is a great way to make your learning more effective. Method 5. Keep the purpose in mind. Concentrate on what is more important. When reading a book, it is better to focus more on what's useful to you, instead of trying to take in all the information you read. Always have a crystal clear purpose of what you are reading and why you're reading. You can start putting this method to use right now, by choosing the methods which seem useful, from this video. Remember this one advice which could help you for the rest of your life. 'The information which is given most importance, stays in your mind' and won't be easily forgotten. All you have to do is, keep an open mind while reading so that you don't miss anything useful. Hope this video helped you remember what you read and learn. Subscribe to this channel for more useful videos. Follow us on Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/constructiv...},
  keywords = {/on halt,learning}
}

